          <p class="eyebrow mb-3">Overview</p>
          <h2 class="section-title">Mission-critical security at the edge</h2>
        </div>
        <div class="prose-content">
          <p>Edge devices deployed in the field face a threat spectrum that fixed data centre infrastructure never encounters: physical capture, tampering attempts, network-level compromise, and prolonged disconnection from central management. Traditional perimeter security assumes a controlled environment — perimeter firewalls, segmented networks, physical access control. Edge devices operate beyond all of these.</p>
          <p>MEAICON's secure edge computing platform applies a defence-in-depth architecture with five interlocking security layers: hardware-rooted trust via TPM 2.0, physical anti-tamper protection with automated response, geo-fencing with location-aware policy enforcement, cryptographic key management including remote zeroization, and secure remote orchestration with chain-of-trust verification. Each layer is independently hardened — compromise at one does not cascade into mission failure.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

